---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="E.R.I.C. Awards 2027"
  description="Categories, prizes, and dates for the E.R.I.C. Awards announced at EUCO Napoli."
>
  <main id="content" class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="kicker">Awards</p>
      <h1>E.R.I.C. Awards, announced at EUCO Napoli</h1>
      <p>Clubs and districts show a finished project. Winners receive money to continue it or to start the next one, plus a trophy at the EUCO gala.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="grid-3">
      <article class="panel">
        <h2>1st</h2>
        <p>200 euro</p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel">
        <h2>2nd</h2>
        <p>150 euro</p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel">
        <h2>3rd</h2>
        <p>100 euro</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <h2>Categories</h2>
    <article class="office">
      <h2>Twin Club Awards</h2>
      <p>At least two clubs from different districts inside the MDIO, a signed twin agreement, and at least one joint project. The applicant club must be an E.R.I.C. member. The prize is paid only to member clubs, split if several of them apply together. Four or more clubs ask social@rotaracteurope.eu for the mega twin certificate.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="office">
      <h2>Best European Service Project</h2>
      <p>A finished service project with a clear community result, aligned with Rotary’s areas of focus.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="office">
      <h2>Rotary and Rotaract collaboration</h2>
      <p>A Rotary club and a Rotaract club that planned and carried out the work together.</p>
    </article>
    <h2>Dates</h2>
    <div class="year"><strong>8 Jan</strong><p>2027. Jury names are published. Objections go to social@rotaracteurope.eu and board@rotaracteurope.eu until 15 January, 23:59 CET.</p></div>
    <div class="year"><strong>17 Jan</strong><p>2027. Applications open.</p></div>
    <div class="year"><strong>17 Mar</strong><p>2027, 23:59 CET. Deadline, about four weeks before EUCO Napoli.</p></div>
    <h2>Rules that catch people out</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The project must already be finished, and it must fall in the current or the previous Rotarian year.</li>
      <li>One project per club in each category. The same project cannot enter two categories.</li>
      <li>A winning project cannot be entered again for five years. A different project can be entered at any time.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The nomination form is still the one on <a href="https://rotaracteurope.eu/impact/eric-awards-2026/">the current awards page</a>.</p>
  </main>
</Base>
